===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|tr|yaşmak}}.<ref>[http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/yashmak "yashmak."] ''Merriam-Webster Online Dictionary.'' Merriam-Webster. 2008.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{hyphenation|en|yash|mak}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[veil]] worn by [[Muslim]] women to cover parts of the face when they are in public.
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1930|author=w:Sax Rohmer|title=The Day the World Ended|year_published=1969|page=ix. 88|passage=Through her gauzy '''''yashmak''''' I could see that she was smiling.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1982|author=w:TC Boyle|title=Water Music|page=46|publisher=Penguin|year_published=2006
|passage=Mungo cannot make out her face, which is concealed behind a '''''yashmak''''' – the double horsehair veil worn by Muslim women in public – but he is immediately struck by her feet and hands.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|veil that covers parts of the face}} {{l|en|niqab}}, {{l|en|veil}}, {{l|en|hijab}}, {{l|en|purdah}}, {{l|en|scarf}}

